QuestGuidance.Register("en",414,{
[13217]="700156B5\n1\tBring an infused garnet to Fastarr\tFastarr has asked you to bring him an infused garnet with which he may be able to aid you in bestowing a quality upon your weapon. He does not, however, know where to find such a stone.\n2\tTalk to Fastarr to travel to the old armoury\tFastarr can be found at the Dolven-view camp in Moria. Fastarr has bidden you to speak with him again when you are ready to seek out the old armoury, but warns you that a well-organized band of Moria Orcs has taken control of the hall.\n3\tBring the empowered garnet to Fastarr\tFastarr can be found at the Dolven-view camp in Moria. You should return to Fastarr to complete the enhancement of your weapon.\n",
[13218]="70051F7D\n1\tCollect Storvâgûn's tarnished emblem of loyalty\tYou have returned to the high cliffs above Helegrod to face Storvâgûn.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have triumphed over Storvâgûn at Helegrod.\n",
[13219]="7006B096\n1\tAsk Mâramit for more traps\tMâramit can be found at Tilmakhím, to the south of Tâkhdar. Ask Mâramit for more traps to place in order to capture pests. Hármelak will pay her later.\n2\tSet traps (total: 5)\tTilmakhím is to the south of Tâkhdar. Lay the traps in various locations around Tilmakhím.\n3\tSpeak with Mâramit\tMâramit can be found at Tilmakhím, to the south of Tâkhdar. Speak with Mâramit and inform her the traps have been laid. She will want you to deliver a message to Hármelak to receive payment for her services.\n4\tReturn to Hármelak\tHármelak is waiting in Dâr Laja. Return to Hármelak to convey Mâramit's good wishes, and inform her the traps have been set.\n",
[13220]="700563D6\n1\tDefeat the Treasure Bugan before it escapes!\t\n2\tDefeat the Treasure Bugan before it escapes! This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\t\n",
[13221]="70061FCB\n1\tComplete to receive your first Coin of the Bugan\tTreasure Bugans have appeared in Instances across Middle-earth!\n2\tComplete to receive your first Coin of the Bugan\tTheodore Gorse (and possibly Treasure Bugans) can be found within any of these instances: Barad Guldur Blood of the Black Serpent Dungeons of Dol Guldur Eithel Gwaur Flight to the Lonely Mountain Fornost: Wraith of Earth Fornost: Wraith of Fire Fornost: Wraith of Shadow Fornost: Wraith of Water Gath Daeroval Glimmerdeep Glinghant Gorthad Nûr Great Barrow: Sambrog Great Barrow: Thadúr Great Barrow: The Maze Haudh Valandil Helegrod: Dragon Wing Helegrod: Drake Wing Helegrod: Giant Wing Helegrod: Spider Wing Inn of the Forsaken Iorbar's Peak Lost Temple Northcotton Farm Ost Dunhoth: Disease Poison Ost Dunhoth: Gortheron Ost Dunhoth: Wound Fear Ost Elendil Sammath Gûl Stoneheight Caverns of Thrumfall Sunken Labyrinth Sword-hall of Dol Guldur Sâri-surma The Battle for Erebor The Bells of Dale The Court of Seregost The Dome of Stars The Dungeons of Naerband The Fires of Smaug The Halls of Night The Harrowing of Morgul The Library at Tham Mírdain The Quays of the Harlond The Ruined City The School at Tham Mírdain The Silent Street Warg-pens of Dol Guldur Webs of the Scuttledells Bar Nirnaeth Ghashan-Kutot The Fallen Kings Askâd-mazal, the Chamber of Shadows Shakalush, the Stair Battle Agoroth, the Narrowdelve Woe of the Willow\n",
[13222]="70009824\n1\tFind the solution to the riddle\tA stone marker in Evendim may hide treasure. Culang told you this riddle, which may hold a clue to the marker's location: \"Two roads pass through green fields. Four kings watch the meeting of the ways.\" You should examine the marker when you find it for some clue to the location of the treasure.\n",
[13223]="7002EF7C\n1\tLet the mysterious old man know that you will defend the herd\tThe mysterious old man is at Éomer's Vengeance, near the eaves of Fangorn, in the Entwash Vale. You should speak again with the mysterious old man if you are willing to defend the herd of wild horses.\n2\tTalk to the mysterious old man at Éomer's Vengeance\tThe mysterious old man is at Éomer's Vengeance, on the eaves of Fangorn, in the Entwash Vale. You should return to the mysterious old man with news of your success.\n3\tTalk to Thane Béortnoth outside of Thornhope\tThane Béortnoth is encamped beyond the walls of Thornhope, east of Éomer's Vengeance. You should return to Thane Béortnoth and tell him of the mysterious old man.\n",
[13224]="70072BF7\n1\tExamine the wooden warning sign\tA wooden sign of warning stands among the trees of Adagím.\n2\tDefeat the trees that move in Adagím (total: 3)\tHuorns of Adagím succumb to the Pale Blight, and you must face them with courage.\n3\tCompleted\tYou proved the match of the walking trees of Adagím.\n",
[13225]="70054661\n1\tBurn webbed trees (total: 10)\tMirkwood spiders have killed and webbed many trees in Taurlingol. You should burn webbed trees.\n2\tTalk to Legolas\tLegolas can be found on a hill near Taurlingol. You should talk to Legolas.\n",
[13226]="7005A6AF\n1\tCollect the skull trophy\tThe skull trophy is located in Rung-shakam. You should steal the skull trophy.\n2\tPlant the skull trophy and defeat Nazdrau\tThe den of Nazdrau can be found in western Azanulbizar. You should plant the skull trophy before Nazdrau's den.\n3\tPlant the skull trophy and defeat Sulthrug\tThe den of Sulthrug can be found in western Azanulbizar. You should plant the skull trophy before Sulthrug's den.\n4\tReturn to Valdi\tValdi can be found in Amdân. You should return to Valdi.\n",
[13227]="70008283\n1\tSearch the Etten Caves for the leader of the trolls\tAngmar's emissary must reside deep within the cave in Taur Gonwaith, south-east of Lin Giliath. You should defeat the emissary of Angmar that has gained the allegiance of the Stone-trolls. NOTE: A fellowship is recommended for this quest.\n2\tDefeat Favargair, Troll-keeper\tAngmar's emissary must reside deep within the cave in Taur Gonwaith, south-east of Lin Giliath. You should defeat the emissary of Angmar that has gained the allegiance of the Stone-trolls. NOTE: A fellowship is recommended for this quest.\n3\tTalk to Thaliollang\tThaliollang is at Lin Giliath, north-west of Taur Gonwaith. Thaliollang will be pleased to know that he was correct in his belief: there was an emissary from Angmar among the trolls. To the benefit of all, you have defeated him.\n",
[13228]="7003EAF8\n1\tDefeat Stone-trolls at Ost-Thondol (total: 8)\tThere are Stone-trolls settled at the ruins of Ost Thondol in the Bruinen Gorges of the Trollshaws. While you are exploring Ost Thondol, you should deal with the Stone-trolls which have settled there.\n",
[13229]="7003ECF5\n1\tDefeat trolls at Taur Gonwaith (total: 10)\tTrolls roam Taur Gonwaith in Meluinen, in the southern North Downs. You should defeat the deadly trolls of Taur Gonwaith.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have defeated a number of menacing, deadly trolls in the woods of Taur Gonwaith.\n",
[13230]="7005B1D9\n1\tDefeat trolls in Vatug-ronk\tDefeating the trolls of Vatug-ronk as quickly as possible before they cause deaths on the battlefield would be best.\n2\tDefeat trolls (total: 5)\tDefeating the trolls of Vatug-ronk as quickly as possible before they cause deaths on the battlefield would be best.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have defeated a number of trolls in Vatug-ronk.\n",
[13231]="700032EA\n1\tDefeat harvest-flies (total: 10)\tThere is a nest of harvest-flies on the Yale-height a distance to the south and east of Budgeford, not far north-east of Woodhall. The hill is marked by three pillars at its pinnacle. Bingo Bolger is disturbed by the increased aggression in the harvest-flies and has asked you to help deal with them.\n2\tTalk to Bingo Bolger\tBingo Bolger is in Budgeford, by a pig pen on the lower slope of the town. Bingo Bolger reported increased aggression among the harvest-flies in the Marish and asked you to deal with them. You should return to him with word of your success.\n",
[13232]="7001AAC7\n1\tTalk to Chief Watcher Grimbriar outside Bree-town\tChief Watcher Grimbriar is at a stone cottage along the roadway, out the West-gate of Bree and north along the Greenway. Graeme Tenderlarch, the mayor of Bree, asked you to speak with Chief Watcher Grimbriar regarding the brigands threatening the safety of Bree-land.\n",
[13233]="7002C48D\n1\tTalk to Gadda, Stanric's most trusted guard\tByrnstan guards the Mead Hall door of Stangard. Gadda stands not far from the Mead Hall. Sabert guards the north gate down below. You should speak with Gadda and see how you may assist the men of Stangard.\n2\tHelp Gadda give food rations out to the men\030Help Sabert by performing a long-overdue watch-tower duty\030Help Byrnstan find what was stolen from him\tGadda guards the Mead Hall in Stangard. You should speak with Gadda about what to do to assist the Men of Stangard.\n3\tTell Gadda of the hardships you observed\tGadda is outside the Mead Hall in Stangard. You should tell Gadda of the many problems and hardships you observed in life at Stangard.\n",
[13234]="70067CB0\n1\tCollect chunks of deldêja from the Irkhadâr Caldera ([see journal]/8)\030Collect bundles of ekhwar from the Irkhadâr Caldera ([see journal]/10)\tThe rich soil around the Irkhadâr Caldera, south of Halrax, promotes the growth of beautiful flowers called, ekhwar. The heat from the volcano long ago forged bits of deldêja desired by the artist Eshen.\n2\tReturn the deldêja and ekhwar to Eshen at Halrax\tYou collected the deldêja chunks and ekhwar flowers Eshen asked you to acquire. Return them to the artist at his home in Halrax.\n3\tPlace the flowers into the dye pot\tEshen asked that you place the flowers into the dye pot near the oven so that he can begin his work.\n4\tSpeak with Eshen\tYou placed the flowers into the dye pot. All that remains to do is speak to Eshen.\n",
[13235]="7000112E\n1\tSearch for the stolen stones among the Stone-trolls\tThe Stone-trolls are encamped on a trail north of the road, further east from the Last Bridge. Tóki Whitebeard asked you to hunt down the trolls who stole the stones and recover the dwarves' treasure.\n2\tSearch for stolen stones among the Stone-trolls of the Trollshaws\tThe Stone-trolls are encamped on a trail north of the road, further east from the Last Bridge. Tóki Whitebeard asked you to hunt down the trolls who stole the stones and recover the treasure.\n3\tBring the stolen stones to Heithur Ironfist\tHeithur Ironfist is at Barachen's camp, south of the road, westward from the Stone-troll camp. You should bring the stolen stones to Heithur Ironfist at once.\n",
[13236]="7001991A\n1\tTalk to a Galadhrim Look-out\tThe Galadhrim Look-outs along the border are waiting to speak with you.\n",
[13237]="7005B509\n1\tTalk to Náin\tNáin waits for you in Aslíf.\n2\tTalk to Náin\tNáin has asked to speak with you in Aslíf.\n",
[13238]="70026F0C\n1\tTalk to Rhodri at the hunters' camp\030Collect turtle-eggs (total: 8)\tTurtle-eggs can be found throughout the southern Dunbog. Rhodri has asked you gather turtle-eggs from all over the southern bog so that the turtles can be saved.\n",
[13239]="7002690F\n1\tRead Orchalwë's journal and reclaim Tham Nambarth\tOrchalwë's journal can be found among your possessions. Orchalwë's journal details what needs be done to reclaim the Fields of Twilight.\n2\tRead Orchalwë's journal and reclaim Tham Varan\tOrchalwë's journal can be found among your possessions. Orchalwë's journal details what needs be done to reclaim the Fields of Twilight.\n3\tRead Orchalwë's journal and reclaim Tham Ornen\tOrchalwë's journal can be found among your possessions. Orchalwë's journal details what needs be done to reclaim the Fields of Twilight.\n4\tRead Orchalwës journal and claim Tham Andalath\tOrchalwë's journal can be found among your possessions. Orchalwë's journal details what needs to be done to reclaim the Fields of Twilight.\n5\tTalk to Orchalwë at Tinnudir\tOrchalwë is at Tinnudir. Orchalwë will be eager to get his journal back and discuss your exploits within the Fields of Twilight.\n",
[13240]="70026169\n1\tCollect twine from the docks (total: 7)\tElf-made twine can be found in Celondim, on and around the docks. You should collect twine from Celondim for the making of shrew-stomping boots.\n2\tBring the twine to Deluraw\tDeluraw, the boot-maker of the Shrew Stomping event, can be found in Duillond near the ovens. You should bring the twine you collected to Deluraw.\n",
[13241]="7000998A\n1\tAccompany Longbough against the Twisted Heart\tLongbough is at the Eavespires, on the north-west shore of Lake Evendim. Longbough asked you to accompany him against the Twisted Heart.\n2\tTalk to Longbough at the Eavespires\tLongbough is at the Eavespires, on the north-west shore of Lake Evendim. You should speak again with Longbough.\n",
[13242]="7000E8BC\n1\tAccompany Longbough against the Twisted Heart\tLongbough is at the Eavespires, on the north-west shore of Lake Evendim. Handarod has asked you to speak with the Ent Longbough and assist him against the Wood-trolls of Evendim.\n2\tTalk to Longbough\tLongbough is at the Eavespires, on the north-west shore of Lake Evendim. You should speak again with Longbough.\n",
[13243]="70042993\n1\tTravel to the West Gate of the town of Bree\tThe town of Bree is to the east along the road from Newbury. Bingo is ready to continue his journey, and wants to walk with you to the West Gate of the town of Bree.\n2\tTalk to Bingo at the West Gate of Bree\tBingo has made a new friend at the West Gate of the town of Bree.\n3\tTalk to Milo Goodbody at the West Gate of Bree\tMilo Goodbody is at the West Gate of Bree. Bingo has made a new friend, a Bree-hobbit named Milo Goodbody, and you should speak with him.\n4\tTalk to Barliman Butterbur inside the Prancing Pony\tYou and Bingo have been invited to partake in the merriment at the Prancing Pony, and should speak to its proprietor, Barliman Butterbur.\n5\tTalk to Bingo in the Prancing Pony\tBingo and Milo have made themselves at home inside the common room of the Prancing Pony.\n6\tSample some food from the large platters (total: 3)\030Drink mugs of ale (total: 3)\030Sing in the common room of the Prancing Pony (quantity: see journal)\tBingo has invited you to eat, drink, and sing in the common room of the Prancing Pony.\n7\tTalk to Bingo in the Prancing Pony\tBingo is enjoying his stay in the common room of the Prancing Pony.\n8\tSample some food from the small platters (total: 2)\030Drink mugs of ale (total: 2)\030Sing in the common room of the Prancing Pony (quantity: see journal)\tBingo has invited you to eat, drink, and sing in the common room of the Prancing Pony.\n9\tTalk to Bingo in the Prancing Pony\tBingo is enjoying his time in the common room of the Prancing Pony.\n10\tBring Bingo's money-purse to Barliman Butterbur\tBarliman Butterbur is the proprietor of the Prancing Pony, and Bingo gave you his money-purse to ensure that he is well-paid for the hospitality.\n11\tTalk to Milo Goodbody in the Prancing Pony\tMilo Goodbody seeks to get your attention in the Prancing Pony.\n12\tClimb on the table and dance\tBingo has asked you to join him on the table and dance!\n13\tBring a few more of Bingo's coins to Barliman Butterbur\tBarliman Butterbur is in the Prancing Pony, and your recent dancing exploits have convinced you that perhaps he deserves a few more of Bingo's coins.\n14\tTalk to Milo Goodbody in the Prancing Pony\tMilo Goodbody is waiting to speak with you in the Prancing Pony.\n15\tFind Bingo somewhere outside the Prancing Pony\tMilo told you that Bingo went outside to get some air, and might be sleeping in one of the haystacks in the stables near the Prancing Pony.\n16\tTravel to the Forsaken Inn, in the Lone-lands\tThe Forsaken Inn is in the Lone-lands, east of Bree. Bingo has decided that it would be best to continue his journey before spending any more time in revelry in the Prancing Pony.\n17\tTalk to Bingo in the Forsaken Inn\tBingo is inside the unwelcoming common room of the Forsaken Inn, in the Lone-lands.\n",
[13244]="7005B116\n1\tDefeat Ufúrzrak Orcs at Muru Azog (total: 14)\030Defeat Ufúrzrak thrug-hai at Muru Azog (total: 4)\030Destroy banners of the Ufúrzrak at Muru Azog (total: 6)\tOrcs, thrug-hai, and banners of the Ufúrzrak clan can be found at Muru Azog. King Thráin has commanded you to join in the assault at Muru Azog. You should aid the Haban'akkâ of Thráin.\n2\tRaise a banner of the Haban'akkâ of Thráin at Muru Azog\tYou have done much to hinder the Ufúrzrak at Muru Azog. You should raise a banner of the Haban'akkâ of Thráin at Muru Azog.\n",
[13245]="7003A4C4\n1\tBring the letter to Guard-captain Thurferth\tGuard-captain Thurferth is near the fountain around the centre of Woodhurst. You should bring the letter to Guard-captain Thurferth.\n2\tBring the letter to Herubrand\tHerubrand is in the cellar of the farmhouse. Herubrand would probably like to see the letter Gifemund prepared for Thurferth.\n",
[13246]="7004D072\n1\tRemove slanderous notices (total: 12)\tDiscrediting notices can be found around Lake-town. You should find and remove any slanderous notices that you come across.\n2\tSuspicious characters can be found around Lake-town. You should find suspicious characters in Lake-town who look to be putting up the slanderous notices.\t\n3\tFind the briber\tSomeone in Lake-town is bribing people to spread rumours. You should find the briber.\n4\tFollow the trail of coins\030Confront the briber\tThe briber in Lake-town has accidentally left a trail of coins behind him. You should follow the trail of coins to catch the briber.\n5\tDefeat Utûkel\tUtûkel can be found in Lake-town's underbelly. You should defeat the one behind the slanderous gossip in Lake-town.\n6\tExamine the thing\tYou should examine what you noticed lying near the defeated Easterling, Utûkel, in Lake-town's underbelly.\n7\tCompleted\tPut a stop to the slanderous gossip in Lake-town.\n",
[13247]="70044641\n1\tCollect mushrooms from the cisterns (total: 16)\tMushrooms can be found within the cisterns. You should collect mushrooms for Rathon.\n2\tSpeak with Rathon\tRathon can be found outside the cistern entrance on the Fourth Circle of Minas Tirith. You should speak with Rathon.\n3\tBring the mushrooms to the rations chest\tThe Foodmongers' Fellow-hall on the First Circle of Minas Tirith. You should bring the mushrooms to a rations chest outside of the Foodmongers' Fellow-hall.\n",
[13248]="7000C37A\n1\tWrite a description of Gollum's cave with Bilbo's writing materials\tGollum's cave is deep within the tunnels of Goblin-town, beyond the central hall. Bilbo Baggins provided you with some writing materials and sent you off to find Gollum's cave, with instruction to verify the details of his book regarding the cave.\n2\tTalk to Bilbo Baggins\tBilbo Baggins is in the Hall of Fire in the Last Homely House at Rivendell, south of Goblin-town. You found Gollum's cave in the depths of Goblin-town and discovered the creature's makeshift hut on an island in the lake. Once there, you wrote down what you saw. Now you should return to Bilbo Baggins.\n",
})
